A fresh task instance requires independent evidence. Treat same-ID references as historical warnings, not transformation rules. For every returned pair, immediately record exact changed coordinates and unaffected candidates, update named hypotheses, and request again only for an observation that separates plausible rules. When invalid-grid feedback arrives, check row count, widths, dimensions, values, and action serialization before making another attempt; keep format diagnosis separate from inference. This session did not establish a reliable transformation for its test, so this reference documents process failures and recovery gates, not a solved output rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-3/play/users/u084/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-evidence-recovery/references/task-29b1b5eb-instance-review.md"}

