{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-evidence-recovery", "file": "references/task-217fc4ad-review.md", "content": "# Session review: premature speculative submissions after multiple demos

This instance supplied six substantially different input/output examples, generally with a full-width or full-height divider and outputs that retained one side/panel in reduced form. No shared deterministic encoding was established by the demos. The test was a 9×2 grid containing 5s and a 7, but repeated guesses alternated among one-column, two-column recolorings, and all-zero outputs; an identical one-column guess was even submitted twice. Those candidates were not supported by exact replay against the demonstrations and all failed.

Reusable recovery lesson: after every rejection, record the exact candidate grid and its hypothesis before acting. Immediately verify the next proposed action is materially different and has evidence; if it is not, stop. Never let attempt-budget pressure or an unresolved task justify arbitrary candidates. On a demo turn, first identify what the new pair adds to the common rule; only request again for a stated discriminator between live hypotheses. This case remained unresolved, so it provides a process warning, not a transformation rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-3/play/users/u084/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-evidence-recovery/references/task-217fc4ad-review.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-incorrect-submission-recovery", "file": "references/path-selection-and-paint.md", "content": "# Separating path selection from recoloring

Straight-line or ray-filling tasks require two distinct inferences: (1) which endpoints/path cells are selected, and (2) which cells on that path change color. Do not assume that every aligned marker pair is connected, that only orthogonal or all eight directions are used, or that every intermediate cell is recolored. For each demonstration, record candidate alignments, intervening cells, old→new values, and aligned candidates that stayed unchanged. Then replay the full rule on immutable input copies and compare every output cell. A wrong result rejects the combined rule; revise endpoint selection and paint behavior as separate hypotheses rather than making cosmetic adjustments to the rendered grid.

Useful test matrix: endpoint color/identity; nearest versus any collinear partner; direction set; intervening-marker blocking; path termination; intermediate cells eligible by color; endpoint preservation; path overlaps. A candidate is ready only when these choices exactly reproduce all demos.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-3/play/users/u084/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-incorrect-submission-recovery/references/path-selection-and-paint.md"}

